As the sun set over Stranglethorn Vale, Glimble Stoneweaver, a gnome Warlock, led his Succubus, Whisper, through the dense jungle. They were on a mission to complete a series of quests for the local goblin faction. Whisper, with her Lesser Invisibility, expertly navigated the treacherous terrain, allowing Glimble to avoid deadly traps and hostile mobs. As they journeyed, Whisper used her Seduction to charm a group of hostile centaurs, giving Glimble time to dispatch them with his trusty dagger.

As they approached the questgiver, a goblin named Gob Grimclaw, Whisper used her Soothing Kiss to calm a nearby pack of vicious spiders, allowing Glimble to complete the quest without incident. With the quest complete, Glimble rewarded Gob with a few gold pieces and a smile. Whisper, content with their successful mission, settled in for a well-deserved rest, her eyes glowing with an otherworldly energy.

Answer: Most Warlocks are seen with Voidwalkers because they are better suited for tanking and threat generation, making them ideal for group content and raids, whereas Succubi are better for soloing and questing due to their crowd control and stealth abilities. [end of text]


